M2 - Timeline width containment and Ctrl+wheel - 2026-10-26

Scope: CompositionTimeline.tsx, useTimelineWheelZoom.ts, composition-editor.css, composition-timeline.css, composition-timeline-viewport.test.tsx.
Static cause: editor grid had no explicit minmax(0,1fr) column; timeline grid/flex chain kept automatic intrinsic minimums while ruler content had an explicit zoomed pixel width. This can enlarge the grid column and push the canvas/control row. Confirmed in source; native pixel geometry was not measured in this slice.
Correction: explicit zero-minimum editor column; min-width:0/max-width:100% in timeline wrapper/root/viewport/control row; scrolling belongs to ruler viewport; responsive control row uses a separate grid group. Buttons remain present.
Ctrl+wheel: non-passive listener on timeline section only, preventDefault only with Ctrl+nonzero vertical delta, viewport pointer anchor when inside; current playhead/visible center fallback outside viewport. Plain wheel behavior retained; listener removed on unmount; current slider updates via shared scale state.
Test harness boundary: Happy DOM WheelEvent omits ctrlKey/clientX/clientY constructor fields, so tests explicitly define those native-event fields. CSS is read from source because Vitest's CSS module stub does not supply computed styles. The CSS test checks resolved style contracts, not rendered pixel bounds or visual approval.

